      "text": [
        " رَأَيْتُ أَبَا الْحَسَنِ ( عليه السلام ) إِذَا تَوَضَّأَ قَبْلَ الطَّعَامِ لَمْ يَمَسَّ الْمِنْدِيلَ وَ إِذَا تَوَضَّأَ بَعْدَ الطَّعَامِ مَسَّ الْمِنْدِيلَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Marazam who said, ",
          "‘I saw Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> when he<sup>asws</sup> performed ablution before the meal, he<sup>asws</sup> did not wipe the towel, and when he<sup>asws</sup> perform ablution after the meal, he<sup>asws</sup> wiped the towel’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Um ay r from Murazim who has said the following: “I saw abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, when making wudu (washing his hands) before food did not wipe his hands with a towel, but he wiped them when he (the Imam) made wudu after food.’” "
        ]
      }
